and the strongest available source image. Build the\r\n208:    prompt with the 12-part `HYPERREALISTIC_IMAGE_SOP.md` framework (see rule\r\n209:    42a): specify skin texture and where pores/imperfections sit, fabric-level\r\n210:    wardrobe, lighting by color temperature, camera/lens, and the anti-AI notes\r\n211:    + negative-prompt clauses that keep it from looking AI-generated. Prompt for\r\n212:    a realistic UGC creator, natural phone-camera texture, believable skin,\r\n213:    no beauty-filter look, no brand logos, and no retained identity. Save the\r\n214:    approved output as `assets/character/creator_hero.png` and the SOP JSON\r\n215:    prompt next to it for reuse across variants.\r\n216: 5. **Generate a reference set.** From the approved hero image, create:\r\n217:    `creator_face.png`, `creator_medium_phone.png`,\r\n218:    `creator_wide_environment.png`, and optionally a 2-3 second idle reference\r\n219:    video. Keep these with `character_card.json`.\r\n220: 6. **Lock seeds and voice.** Store `visual_seed` for Seedance and `voice_seed`\r\n221:    or `voice_id` for ElevenLabs. Reuse the same seed/reference set for every\r\n222:    clip in a batch; vary only shot actions, hook text, and CTA.\r\n223: 7. **Produce clips with Seedance 2.0 through fal.ai.** Use\r\n224:    `tools/fal_seedance_video.py generate --mode reference --seed <visual_seed>`\r\n225:    plus `--reference-image` for the approved creator references. Pass\r\n226:    `--reference-audio` when native Seedance audio/lip movement is intentional,\r\n227:    or use a separate ElevenLabs voice track for controlled ad narration. Prompt\r\n228:    each beat as a phone-native scene: creator talking to camera, holding\r\n229:    product, screen demo, over-the-shoulder app use, reaction shot,\r\n230:    receipt/proof shot, CTA close.\r\n231: 8. **Assemble like a UGC ad.** First frame must communicate the hook before\r\n232:    the viewer reads the caption. Use jump cuts, pattern interrupts, large\r\n233:    bottom captions, product/UI inserts, quick proof overlays, and no dead air.\r\n234: 9. **QC for believability, audio, visuals, and compliance.** Reject face drift,\r\n235:    too-polished skin, uncanny hands/teeth, lip-sync mismatch, fake platform\r\n236:    logos, blank phone screens, unreadable/generated product UI, impossible\r\n237:    product claims, and any testimonial wording that implies a real customer\r\n238:    experience unless the user provided that experience. For reference-inspired\r\n239:    ads, run `tools/ad_quality_gate.py` and inspect the second-by-second\r\n240:    reference/candidate sheet plus all dense risky-window sheets.\r\n241: 10. **Export test variants.** Render `9:16` masters first, plus `1:1` or `4:5`\r\n242:     if requested. Save `variant_matrix.json`, final MP4s, captions, character\r\n243:     references, seeds, prompts, and QC notes in the job folder.\r\n244: \r\n245: UGC hook families to use before writing the body:\r\n246: \r\n247: - **Confession:** \"I almost didn't try this because...\"\r\n248: - **Contrarian:** \"Stop doing <common behavior> if you want <outcome>.\"\r\n249: - **Problem-callout:** \"If <pain> keeps happening, check this first.\"\r\n250: - **Receipt/proof:** \"I tested <thing> for <timeframe>, here is what changed.\"\r\n251: - **Demo-first:** \"Watch what happens when I do <specific action>.\"\r\n252: - **Speedrun:** \"I fixed <pain> in <short timeframe> with three steps.\"\r\n253: - **Before/after:** \"This was my <messy state>; this is it after <product/action>.\"\r\n254: - **Curiosity gap:** \"The weird part is not <obvious thing>; it is <specific mechanism>.\"\r\n255: \r\n256: UGC body patterns:\r\n257: \r\n258: - **Pain -> tiny demo -> payoff -> CTA.**\r\n259: - **Old way -> new way -> proof -> CTA.**\r\n260: - **Mistake -> correction -> product mechanism -> CTA.**\r\n261: - **Skeptic -> test -> result -> objection -> CTA.**\r\n262: \r\n263: Seedance prompt skeleton:\r\n264: \r\n265: ```text\r\n266: Handheld vertical phone video. Fictional UGC creator from reference images,\r\n267: same face, same hair, same wardrobe family, natural skin texture, no beauty\r\n268: filter. <specific beat action>. Real <home office / kitchen / parked car /\r\n269: desk> environment, natural light, casual speech energy, slight handheld motion,\r\n270: believable phone-camera exposure. No logos, no subtitles in the footage, no\r\n271: perfect studio lighting, no face morphing, no extra people.\r\n272: ```\r\n273: \r\n274: After HeyGen renders the avatar, immediately:\r\n275: \r\n276: 1. Extract the avatar audio with FFmpeg (`-vn -acodec libmp3lame`).\r\n277: 2. Transcribe with OpenAI Whisper (`response_format=verbose_json`, `timestamp_granularities=['word','segment']`) to get word- and segment-level timestamps.\r\n278: 3. Inspect the segments. If the script is duplicated, set the avatar trim end to the last second of the first unique pass.\r\n279: 4. Build a `storyboard.json` mapping each segment to a layout (avatar fullscreen / b-roll PiP / browser PiP), a visual job, a surface, a before/action/after description, a source-deck asset, a chapter title, and a source attribution.\r\n280: 5. Use those exact timestamps everywhere downstream — captions, segment cuts, lower-thirds.\r\n281: \r\n282: ### Stage 3: Asset generation\r\n283: \r\n284: Use the routing rules:\r\n285: \r\n286: - HeyGen for presenter/avatar clips.\r\n287: - Seedance 2.0 for cinematic b-roll and generated motion.\r\n288: - Seedance 2.0 reference-image + seed mode for UGC character-consistent clips.\r\n289: - OpenAI image generation/editing for storyboards, stills, thumbnails, inserts, and fictional UGC creator references.\r\n290: - `agent_browser_recorder.py` for coherent agent-operated browser footage.\r\n291: - `screen_recorder.py` for lower-level product walkthrough recordings.\r\n292: - `local_explainer_broll.py` as a no-credit fallback when fal/Seedance is unavailable.\r\n293: - ElevenLabs for voiceover and music when available.\r\n294: \r\n295: ### Stage 4: Timeline assembly\r\n296: \r\n297: Choose the composition engine:\r\n298: \r\n299: - Remotion for React timelines, reusable product mockups, captioned talking head, b-roll overlays, and browser preview.\r\n300: - HyperFrames for HTML-native timelines, deterministic frame capture, GSAP/Lottie/CSS animations, and agent-friendly browser preview.\r\n301: - FFmpeg for practical compositing, muxing, chroma key, subtitles, audio, and final platform exports.\r\n302: \r\n303: ### Stage 5: QC and export\r\n304: \r\n305: Always check:\r\n306: \r\n307: - video has a video stream and expected resolution,\r\n308: - audio exists when expected,\r\n309: - duration is within target,\r\n310: - captions are readable and synced,\r\n311: - no obvious black frames,\r\n312: - final codec is compatible: `libx264`, `aac`, `yuv420p`.\r\n313: - b-roll layout QC contact sheets were reviewed and all non-passing assets were fixed/replaced.\r\n314: \r\n315: ## Main tools\r\n316: \r\n317: ```bash\r\n318: python3 .agents/skills/super-video-maker/tools/video_recipes.py list\r\n319: python3 .agents/skills/super-video-maker/tools/video_recipes.py test\r\n320: python3 .agents/skills/super-video-maker/tools/heygen_client.py\r\n321: python3 .agents/skills/super-video-maker/tools/fal_seedance_video.py generate --mode reference --prompt \"@Image1 handheld UGC creator...\" --duration 7 --resolution 1080p --aspect-ratio 16:9 --reference-image assets/character/creator_hero.png\r\n322: python3 .agents/skills/super-video-maker/tools/fal_seedance_video.py generate --mode reference --prompt \"@Image1 and @Image2 show the same fictional creator. Handheld vertical phone video...\" --duration 5 --resolution 720p --aspect-ratio 9:16 --seed 18427 --reference-image assets/character/creator_hero.png --reference-image assets/character/creator_medium_phone.png\r\n323: python3 .agents/skills/super-video-maker/tools/image_provider.py edit --reference-image real_person_reference.jpg --prompt \"Create a distinct fictional UGC creator...\" --size 1024x1536 --quality high --input-fidelity high --model gpt-image-2\r\n324: python3 .agents/skills/super-video-maker/tools/agent_browser_recorder.py\r\n325: python3 .agents/skills/super-video-maker/tools/local_explainer_broll.py\r\n326: python3 .agents/skills/super-video-maker/tools/screen_recorder.py\r\n327: python3 .agents/skills/super-video-maker/tools/demo_video_composer.py\r\n328: python3 .agents/skills/super-video-maker/tools/video_captioner.py\r\n329: python3 .agents/skills/super-video-maker/tools/ffmpeg_qc.py\r\n330: python3 .agents/skills/super-video-maker/tools/broll_layout_qc.py\r\n331: ```\r\n332: \r\n333: ## Result contract\r\n334: \r\n335: Each stage should end with one line:\r\n336: \r\n337: ```json\r\n338: RESULT: {\"status\":\"succeeded\",\"stage\":\"asset_generation\",\"job_id\":\"video_001\",\"artifacts\":[{\"type\":\"video\",\"path\":\"output_videos/clip.mp4\"}],\"metrics\":{\"duration_seconds\":7,\"aspect_ratio\":\"16:9\"},\"next_action\":\"assemble_timeline\"}\r\n339: ```\r\n340: \r\n341: On failure:\r\n342: \r\n343: ```json\r\n344: RESULT: {\"status\":\"failed\",\"stage\":\"asset_generation\",\"error\":\"friendly explanation\",\"debug_log\":\"tmp/video_jobs/video_001/log.txt\"}\r\n345: ```\r\n346: \r\n347: ## Provider defaults\r\n348: \r\n349: - Avatar: HeyGen.\r\n350: - AI video b-roll: fal.ai `bytedance/seedance-2.0/reference-to-video` or `bytedance/seedance-2.0/fast/reference-to-video`.\r\n351: - Images: OpenAI image generation/editing.\r\n352: - Voice: ElevenLabs.\r\n353: - Music: ElevenLabs Music first, then Replicate or Suno adapters if configured.\r\n354: - Programmatic editor: Remotion.\r\n355: - HTML-native editor: HyperFrames.\r\n356: - Final render/QC: FFmpeg and ffprobe.\r\n357: \r\n358: ## When not to use this skill\r\n359: \r\n360: - The user only wants a single image.\r\n361: - The user only wants a plain transcript with no video work.\r\n362: - The user asks for manual Premiere/DaVinci steps and does not want automation.\r\n363: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
