{"step_index":463,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T16:20:33Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-23T21:50:33+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-23T21:50:48+05:30\n\nThe command exited with code 0.\nOutput:\n<truncated 50 lines>\nservices such as Discord, Telegram, WhatsApp, and Google Chat.\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:76:- **VRAM / RAM Adjuster** by *g3n3rativ3* - Tune how much graphics and system memory WanGP uses \r\nwithout manually editing configuration files.\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:77:- **Wildcards** by *GKartist* - Add reusable variables and random choices to prompts so you can \r\nquickly produce controlled variations.\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:78:\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:79:**New Wan2GP Desktop Installer** - [Wan2GP \r\nDesktop](https://github.com/GKartist75/wan2gp-desktop) by GKArtist lets you install, update, and launch WanGP from a \r\nsingle window. It handles Git, Python, CUDA, and PyTorch setup for you, making it the easiest way to get started on \r\nWindows.\r\n> Wan2GP\\README.md:241:The 1-click automated scripts for both **Windows (`.bat`)** and **Linux/macOS (`.sh`)** make \r\ninstallation, environment management, and updates as seamless as possible. These scripts will not only install WanGP \r\nbut also best acceleration kernels (Triton, Sage, Flash, GGuf, Lightx2v, Nunchaku) available for your config.\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:242:\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:243:*?? **Windows Users:** Double-click the `.bat` files. **Linux Users:** Run the `.sh` files in \r\nyour terminal.*\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:244:\r\n> Wan2GP\\README.md:245:#### **1?? Installation (`scripts\\install.bat` | `scripts/install.sh`)**\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:246:\r\n> Wan2GP\\README.md:247:**Choose Installation Type**\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:248:- **Auto Install**\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:249:- **Manual Install**\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:250:\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:251:**Manual Install**\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:252:\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:253:If you selected Manual Install, you will be guided through:\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:254:\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:255:1. **Choose your package manager**\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:256:2. **Name your environment**\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:257:3. **Select your Install Mode**\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:258:\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:259:#### 2?? Starting the App (`scripts\\run.bat` | `scripts/run.sh`)\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:260:Once installed, use this script to launch the application. It runs WAN2GP using your active \r\nenvironment.\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:261:\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:262:*   **?? Customizing Launch Arguments (`args.txt`)**\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:263:    *   If you want to pass extra command-line flags to the launcher (like enabling advanced UI \r\nfeatures or automatically opening your browser), create an `args.txt` file in your `scripts` folder.\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:264:    *   **Example `args.txt`:**\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:265:        ```text\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:266:        --advanced --open-browser\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:267:        ```\r\n> Wan2GP\\README.md:295:### Manual installation: (for RTX20xx - RTX50xx)\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:296:\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:297:```bash\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:298:git clone https://github.com/deepbeepmeep/Wan2GP.git\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:299:cd Wan2GP\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:300:conda create -n wan2gp python=3.11.14\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:301:conda activate wan2gp\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:302:pip install torch==2.10.0 torchvision==0.25.0 torchaudio==2.10.0 --index-url \r\nhttps://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu130\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:303:pip install -r requirements.txt\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:304:```\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:305:\r\n> Wan2GP\\README.md:306:### Manual installation: (for GTX 10xx)\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:307:\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:308:```bash\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:309:git clone https://github.com/deepbeepmeep/Wan2GP.git\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:310:cd Wan2GP\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:311:conda create -n wan2gp python=3.10.9\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:312:conda activate wan2gp\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:313:pip install torch==2.7.1 torchvision==0.22.1 torchaudio==2.7.1 --index-url \r\nhttps://download.pytorch.org/whl/test/cu128\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:314:pip install -r requirements.txt\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:315:```\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:316:\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:317:#### Run the application:\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:318:\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:319:```bash\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:320:python wgp.py\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:321:```\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:322:If you are low on VRAM, there is a trick to increase the amount of VRAM available (between 1GB \r\nand 5GB of VRAM to be gained depending on the GPU): *disable GPU Usage in your Web Browser*.\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:323:\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:324:Run *scripts/start-chrome-no-gpu.bat* or *scripts/start-chrome-no-gpu.sh* to launch Chrome \r\nwithout using your GPU. \r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:325:\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:326:First time using WanGP ? Just check the *Guides* tab, and you will find a selection of \r\nrecommended models to use.\r\n> Wan2GP\\README.md:353:Once you are done you will have to reinstall *Sage Attention*, *Triton*, *Flash Attention*. \r\nCheck the **[Installation Guide](docs/INSTALLATION.md)** -\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:354:\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:355:if you get some error messages related to git, you may try the following (beware this will \r\noverwrite local changes made to the source code of WanGP):\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:356:```bash\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:357:git fetch origin && git reset --hard origin/main\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:358:conda activate wan2gp\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:359:pip install -r requirements.txt\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:360:```\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:361:When you have the confirmation it works well you can then delete the old conda env:\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:362:```bash\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:363:conda uninstall -n old_wan2gp --all  \r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:364:```\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:365:\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:366:#### Run headless (batch processing):\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:367:\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:368:Process saved queues without launching the web UI:\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:369:```bash\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:370:# Process a saved queue\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:371:python wgp.py --process my_queue.zip\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:372:```\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:373:Create your queue in the web UI, save it with \"Save Queue\", then process it headless. See [CLI \r\nDocumentation](docs/CLI.md) for details.\r\n> Wan2GP\\README.md:402:## ?? Installation\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:403:\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:404:### Nvidia\r\n> Wan2GP\\README.md:405:For detailed installation instructions for different GPU generations:\r\n> Wan2GP\\README.md:406:- **[Installation Guide](docs/INSTALLATION.md)** - Complete setup instructions for RTX 10XX to \r\nRTX 50XX\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:407:\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:408:### AMD\r\n> Wan2GP\\README.md:409:For detailed installation instructions for different GPU generations:\r\n> Wan2GP\\README.md:410:- **[Installation Guide](docs/AMD-INSTALLATION.md)** - Complete setup instructions for RDNA 4, \r\n3, 3.5, and 2\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:411:\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:412:## ?? Usage\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:413:\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:414:### Basic Usage\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:415:- **[Getting Started Guide](docs/GETTING_STARTED.md)** - First steps and basic usage\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:416:- **[Models Overview](docs/MODELS.md)** - Available models and their capabilities\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:417:- **[Prompts Guide](docs/PROMPTS.md)** - How WanGP interprets prompts, images as prompts, \r\nenhancers, and macros\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:418:\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:419:### Advanced Features\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:420:- **[Deepy Assistant](docs/DEEPY.md)** - Enable Deepy, configure its tool presets, use selected \r\nmedia and frames, and run Deepy from the CLI\r\n  Wan2GP\\README.md:421:- **[Loras Guide](docs/LORAS.md)** - Using and managing Loras for customization\r\n  Wan2GP\\READ